### Try the payment endpoints (IntelliJ HTTP Client). Select the "local" environment.
###
### Before you start:
###   docker compose up -d postgres meridian-mock
###   cd payments-api && mvn spring-boot:run        (or run PaymentsApiApplication in IntelliJ)
###
### Run the requests top to bottom. Requests 2 to 5 share one Idempotency-Key.
### Payments start PDNG; the mock then calls the webhook and they move to ACCP (or RJCT). Re-run request 5 to see it.


### 0. Health check
GET {{apiUrl}}/actuator/health


### 1. Pick a single-use token (this request just checks health again and generates the token). Tokenisation happens before our API and is out of scope,
### so any new tok_... value works with the Meridian mock. The prefix chooses the outcome:
###   tok_decline_funds (AM04) | tok_decline_blocked (AC04) | tok_decline_invalid (FF01)
###   tok_decline_other (NARR) | tok_slow (accepted after 3 minutes) | anything else: accepted
< {%
    client.global.set("token", "tok_" + Date.now());
%}
GET {{apiUrl}}/actuator/health


### 2. Submit a payment (new Idempotency-Key). Expect 202 and status PDNG.
< {%
    client.global.set("key", "demo-" + Date.now());
%}
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{key}}

{ "token": "{{token}}", "amount": { "value": "125.50", "currency": "GBP" } }

> {%
    client.global.set("paymentId", response.body.id);
    client.test("accepted and pending", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 202, "expected 202");
        client.assert(response.body.status === "PDNG", "expected PDNG");
        client.assert(response.body.cancellable === true, "expected cancellable");
    });
%}


### 3. Repeat request 2 exactly. Expect 202 and the SAME payment id (no second payment).
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{key}}

{ "token": "{{token}}", "amount": { "value": "125.50", "currency": "GBP" } }

> {%
    client.test("same payment returned", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 202, "expected 202");
        client.assert(response.body.id === client.global.get("paymentId"), "expected the original payment");
    });
%}


### 4. Same key, different amount. Expect 409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_CONFLICT.
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{key}}

{ "token": "{{token}}", "amount": { "value": "999.00", "currency": "GBP" } }

> {%
    client.test("conflict", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "expected 409");
        client.assert(response.body.code === "IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_CONFLICT", "expected IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_CONFLICT");
    });
%}


### 5. Read the payment back (from our database). Expect 200.
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}


### 6. Supported currencies
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/currencies


### ---------- Error cases ----------

### 7. Wrong amount format (one decimal). Expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR.
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-bad-format-{{$timestamp}}

{ "token": "tok_whatever", "amount": { "value": "125.5", "currency": "GBP" } }


### 8. Zero amount. Expect 422 INVALID_AMOUNT.
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-zero-{{$timestamp}}

{ "token": "tok_whatever", "amount": { "value": "0.00", "currency": "GBP" } }


### 9. Amount above the maximum (10000.00). Expect 422 INVALID_AMOUNT.
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-big-{{$timestamp}}

{ "token": "tok_whatever", "amount": { "value": "10000.01", "currency": "GBP" } }


### 10. Currency Meridian cannot take (no decimals). Expect 422 CURRENCY_NOT_SUPPORTED.
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-jpy-{{$timestamp}}

{ "token": "tok_whatever", "amount": { "value": "500.00", "currency": "JPY" } }


### 11. Missing Idempotency-Key. Expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR.
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "tok_whatever", "amount": { "value": "10.00", "currency": "GBP" } }


### 12. Token Meridian rejects (the mock refuses anything not shaped like tok_...). Expect 422 PROVIDER_REJECTED (the payment is saved as RJCT).
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-badtoken-{{$timestamp}}

{ "token": "not-a-token", "amount": { "value": "10.00", "currency": "GBP" } }


### 13. Reuse the token from request 1 with a NEW key. Tokens are single-use, so expect 422 PROVIDER_REJECTED.
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-reuse-{{$timestamp}}

{ "token": "{{token}}", "amount": { "value": "125.50", "currency": "GBP" } }


### 14. Cancel the payment from request 2. Expect 200 and status CANC.
### (Run it soon after request 2: the mock settles payments after 30 seconds, and then the cancel gives 409.)
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/cancellation

> {%
    client.test("cancelled", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "expected 200");
        client.assert(response.body.status === "CANC", "expected CANC");
    });
%}


### 15. Cancel it again. Expect 200 and CANC again (cancel is idempotent).
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/cancellation


### 16. Unknown payment id. Expect 404 PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND.
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
